#!arguments-desc = Weather.Replace: [Weather] Replacement Scope\n    ├ OFF: Disabled\n    ├ CN: Mainland China\n    ├ CN|HK|MO|TW: Mainland China, Hong Kong, Macau, and Taiwan\n    └ .*: All Regions\nReplace weather data only for matching regions. Keep Disabled when you only need AQI replacement.\n\nWeather.Provider: [Weather] Data Source\n    ├ WeatherKit: WeatherKit (No replacement)\n    ├ OpenWeather: OpenWeather\n    └ QWeather: QWeather\nUse the selected provider to replace weather data.\n\nWeather.Fallback.Provider: [Weather] OpenWeather Fallback\n    ├ WeatherKit: WeatherKit\n    └ QWeather: QWeather\nFallback provider used when OpenWeather weather data is unavailable or rate-limited.\n\nNextHour.Provider: [Next-Hour Precipitation Intensity] Data Source\n    ├ WeatherKit: WeatherKit (Do not add)\n    ├ OpenWeather: OpenWeather\n    └ QWeather: QWeather\nUse the selected provider to replace or fill next-hour precipitation intensity data.\n\nNextHour.Fallback.Provider: [Next-Hour Precipitation Intensity] OpenWeather Fallback\n    ├ WeatherKit: WeatherKit\n    └ QWeather: QWeather\nFallback provider used when OpenWeather next-hour precipitation data is unavailable or rate-limited.\n\nAirQuality.Replace: [Air Quality] Replacement Scope\n    ├ CN: Mainland China\n    ├ CN|HK|MO|TW: Mainland China, Hong Kong, Macau, and Taiwan\n    └ .*: All Regions\nReplace air-quality data only for matching regions.\n\nAirQuality.Provider: [Air Quality] Data Source\n    ├ WeatherKit: WeatherKit (No replacement)\n    ├ IQAir: IQAir\n    ├ QWeather: QWeather\n    └ WAQI: WAQI\nUse the selected provider to replace AQI. IQAir results can be supplemented by the configured fallback providers when pollutant details are missing.\n\nAirQuality.Pollutants.Provider: [Air Quality] Pollutants Source\n    ├ Auto: Auto\n    ├ IndexProvider: Same as AQI Source\n    ├ WeatherKit: WeatherKit\n    ├ IQAir: IQAir\n    ├ QWeather: QWeather\n    └ WAQI: WAQI\nChoose where pollutant concentrations come from. Auto avoids extra requests for Provider Default AQI, and fetches fallback pollutants only when US or China AQI recalculation needs them.\n\nAirQuality.Standard: [Air Quality] AQI Standard\n    ├ Provider: Provider Default\n    ├ US: US AQI (EPA NowCast)\n    └ CN: China AQI (HJ 633-2012)\nChoose the AQI standard used for display. Provider Default keeps the selected provider's own AQI; US or China recalculates AQI from pollutant concentrations when available.\n\nAirQuality.RequestTimeout: [Air Quality] Request Timeout\nMaximum wait time in milliseconds for each third-party AQI provider before falling back or keeping the original WeatherKit response.\n\nAirQuality.Fallback.Provider: [Air Quality] Fallback Sources\n    ├ QWeather: QWeather\n    └ WAQI: WAQI\nFallback order used when the primary AQI provider is unavailable. Pollutant details are fetched from fallback providers only when a forced AQI standard needs them.\n\nAPI.OpenWeather.URL: [API] OpenWeather Request URL\nOpenWeather One Call API 4.0 request URL\n\nAPI.OpenWeather.Token: [API] OpenWeather Token\nOpenWeather API token\n\nAPI.QWeather.Host: [API] QWeather Host\nHostname used by the QWeather API\n\nAPI.QWeather.Token: [API] QWeather Token\nQWeather API token\n\nAPI.IQAir.URL: [API] IQAir Request URL\nIQAir AirVisual API request URL\n\nAPI.IQAir.Token: [API] IQAir Token\nIQAir AirVisual API token\n\nAPI.WAQI.Token: [API] WAQI Token\nWAQI API token. Leave empty to let the script try the public nearest-station flow.\n\nStorage: [Storage] Configuration Type\n    ├ Argument: Prefer configuration passed by $argument, such as plugin options and module arguments. Missing $argument values are provided by PersistentStore (BoxJs).\n    ├ PersistentStore: Only use configuration from $persistentStore, such as BoxJs.\n    └ database: Only use defaults from the author's database.mjs file. Other custom configuration will no longer take effect.\nChoose the configuration source. For legacy setups without this option, the order remains $persistentStore (BoxJs) > $argument > database.\n\nLogLevel: [Debug] Log Level\n    ├ OFF: Off\n    ├ ERROR: Error\n    ├ WARN: Warning\n    ├ INFO: Info\n    ├ DEBUG: Debug\n    └ ALL: All\nChoose the script log level. Logs below the selected level will be suppressed.\n

